<title>SWEDEN: Lamfalussy says fiscal coordination needed.</title>
<headline>Lamfalussy says fiscal coordination needed.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Institute (EMI) head Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Tuesday that substantial coordination of fiscal policies would be needed after the EU's Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) is launched.  </p>
<p>&quot;There will be demand for substantial coordination of fiscal policies (but), that does not mean in any way identical fiscal policies,&quot; Lamfalussy told a Swedish parliamentary committee.</p>
<p>However Lamfalussy said taxation systems did not need to be coordinated between EMU members.</p>
<p>He said monetary policy changes could not create higher growth in the long term -- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
